WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(crowd applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- All right everybody, let's finish up

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.730
with a heartwarming story.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.140
I'm pretty sure you're gonna love.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.159
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.159 --> 00:00:06.727
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.727 --> 00:00:08.730
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.690
For six years, retired California
Fire Captain Shane Porter

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.400
bonded with his sons working together

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.700
to restore a 1969 Jeepster.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.280
It was a passion project
that came to a halt last year

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.050
when Shane passed away,

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.110
that is until a local high
school teacher volunteered

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.540
to have his class take over the project.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.390
Now, a year later, the
Jeep looks brand new,

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.730
and Shane's family
couldn't be more grateful.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.100
We have Shane's wife,
Tigger, on the line right now

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.200
along with Bob, the high school teacher

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.520
who took on the project.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.380
They watch on NBC Four Los Angeles.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.442
What's going on y'all?

00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:43.347
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:44.460
- Hey, hey.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.960
Hi, Kelly!

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.510
- Oh my gosh, that Jeepster is so cool.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.700
So, Bob, how did this all start?

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.580
- Well, everyone knows
the Porter family in town.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.660
They're an amazing family,

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.800
and they do so much for their community

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.420
and so much for the school district,

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.920
and I've known them for years.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.650
When Shane passed away, I was
helping Tigger at the house,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.270
saw the Jeepster in the garage,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.610
and she told me about
the restoration project.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.160
I'm an automotive technology instructor,

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.300
and I came back to my class,
talked to my advanced class,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.150
and they said, we have to
do this for the family.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.560
It was not even a question.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.570
We did a 15-month restoration on it,

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.730
and when we gave it back to the family,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.140
it was a very emotional day,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.300
and there wasn't a dry eye in the house.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.660
- Oh my gosh, what a special
class of kids you got.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.220
That's amazing, and Tigger,

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.370
what a beautiful surprise for you, right?

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.720
- Oh, yes, yes.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.553
You know what?

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:36.870
These kids had no idea
who I was, what we did,

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.070
what, you know, I'm a paramedic,

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.070
and they have no idea, you
know, anything about us,

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.960
but they did this out of
the kindness of their heart,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.260
and they did this because
of Bobby's teaching.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.320
My boys are gone now.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.900
My oldest is in the Air Force,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.233
and my youngest is in the Army, and Shane.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.480
So, I'm alone now.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.240
So, when I need it the most,
I just get in the Jeep,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.683
and I drive, and it's like
we're all together again.

00:02:02.683 --> 00:02:03.516
(crowd sighing)

00:02:03.516 --> 00:02:08.227
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:11.100
- I mean, I love that
life works out like that,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.480
and by the way, thank you so much.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.880
Please tell your sons thank
you so much for their service,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.713
first of all.

00:02:15.713 --> 00:02:16.546
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:02:16.546 --> 00:02:18.210
Now, you have this beautiful reminder.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.610
Every time you get in this
vehicle, like they're still

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.710
with you in some way.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.230
Bob, thank you so much for being
such an incredible teacher.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.730
First of all, teachers
make the world go 'round.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.229
So, thank you for that.

00:02:28.229 --> 00:02:29.062
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:02:29.062 --> 00:02:31.380
Your class is incredible.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.110
Tigger, you probably look
so badass in that Jeepster.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.850
I'm not kidding, girl,
you probably look so fly

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.810
driving around in that.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.340
I'm like, I'm not only liking,

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.379
I'm loving your post right
now, guys, all right?

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:41.212
(post dinging)

00:02:41.212 --> 00:02:42.045
- [Tigger] Oh.

00:02:42.045 --> 00:02:42.878
- [Bob] Thank you.

00:02:42.878 --> 00:02:43.711
- [Tigger] Thank you, thank you.

00:02:43.711 --> 00:02:44.544
- And that's not all.

00:02:44.544 --> 00:02:46.290
Our season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.210
makers of friXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.320
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.360
want to celebrate teachers, like Bob,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.790
instilling such kindness
and thoughtfulness

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:54.630
into his students.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.780
So, they are giving
Bob a thousand dollars.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.613
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:02:57.613 --> 00:02:58.446
Just for being amazing.

00:02:58.446 --> 00:02:59.279
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.112
- Yeah!

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:02.070
That's so cool!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.312
- Thank you guys so much!

00:03:04.312 --> 00:03:05.145
Beautiful, beautiful people.

00:03:05.145 --> 00:03:06.720
Thank you for joining us.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.340
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.129
Josh Gad, Andrew Rannells,
Davido, and Nicole Avant.

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.451
Y'all have a great day, and if it's not,

00:03:13.451 --> 00:03:14.951
try and change it.

